1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,629
Welcome to Melody and
Barnaby's Music Nuggets!

2
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:11,363
Today we are going to learn
about long and short notes.

3
00:00:13,363 --> 00:00:17,657
Remember the beat? We count
four beats in every bar.

4
00:00:17,857 --> 00:00:18,507
One.

5
00:00:18,557 --> 00:00:19,300
Two.

6
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:20,139
Three.

7
00:00:20,189 --> 00:00:21,389
Four.

8
00:00:24,432 --> 00:00:27,658
Some notes last… one beat.

9
00:00:28,258 --> 00:00:31,809
This note is called… a crotchet.

10
00:00:32,409 --> 00:00:36,563
In America… it is
called a quarter note.

11
00:00:39,363 --> 00:00:42,868
Four crotchets… fill the bar.

12
00:00:46,068 --> 00:00:49,433
Some notes last longer… Listen.

13
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:54,838
This note lasts two beats…
It is called a minim.

14
00:00:57,438 --> 00:01:01,638
In America… it is called a half note.

15
00:01:04,438 --> 00:01:07,525
Two minims… fill the bar.

16
00:01:10,725 --> 00:01:14,694
The longest note… lasts four beats.

17
00:01:15,294 --> 00:01:18,752
It is called… a semibreve.

18
00:01:19,352 --> 00:01:23,274
In America… it is called a whole note.

19
00:01:26,074 --> 00:01:30,646
It fills the whole bar…
so it is a whole note.

20
00:01:33,846 --> 00:01:40,787
Two minims… are half a bar
each… so a minim is a half note.

21
00:01:43,987 --> 00:01:45,767
Four crotchets…

22
00:01:45,817 --> 00:01:48,647
are a quarter of a bar each…

23
00:01:48,697 --> 00:01:52,275
so a crotchet is a quarter note.

24
00:01:55,475 --> 00:01:58,329
One bar… three ways.

25
00:02:01,929 --> 00:02:03,994
Clap and count with me!

26
00:02:04,494 --> 00:02:05,144
One.

27
00:02:05,194 --> 00:02:05,937
Two.

28
00:02:05,987 --> 00:02:06,776
Three.

29
00:02:06,826 --> 00:02:08,026
Four.

30
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:09,820
One.

31
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:10,613
Two.

32
00:02:10,663 --> 00:02:11,452
Three.

33
00:02:11,502 --> 00:02:12,702
Four.

34
00:02:13,845 --> 00:02:14,495
One.

35
00:02:14,545 --> 00:02:15,288
Two.

36
00:02:15,338 --> 00:02:16,128
Three.

37
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:17,378
Four.

38
00:02:20,421 --> 00:02:23,322
Your turn! Look at the notes.

39
00:02:23,822 --> 00:02:27,372
How many beats… does this note last?

40
00:02:31,672 --> 00:02:32,872
Two.

41
00:02:34,655 --> 00:02:36,766
What is this note called?

42
00:02:40,866 --> 00:02:44,695
A crotchet… or a quarter note.

43
00:02:46,495 --> 00:02:48,467
Is this bar full?

44
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:55,607
No! One beat is missing.

45
00:02:56,507 --> 00:02:57,829
You've got it!

46
00:02:59,529 --> 00:03:00,990
Now it's your turn!

47
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:05,019
Play How Long Is the
Note and match the beats!

48
00:03:06,819 --> 00:03:10,740
Grown-ups, subscribe so
you never miss a Nugget.

49
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:14,317
New ones every Wednesday and Saturday.

50
00:03:14,617 --> 00:03:17,007
See you for the next Nugget!

